# Manifest for bin/run-examples. One line per example program, in run order.
#
#   script  [stdin=FILE] [args=a,b,c] [needs=net] [timeout=N] [skip="why"]
#           [known="why"] [expect-stderr=1] [expect_exit=N]
#
# Paths in stdin= are relative to the script's own directory. Scripts run from
# their own directory in a scratch copy, so files they write are discarded.
#   skip=   don't run it at all (interactive, needs special hardware, ...)
#   known=  a known problem; reported as KNOWN, and flagged FIXED once it passes
#   needs=net  needs the Internet; skipped with --offline
#   slow=1     takes a long time; skipped with --quick

